<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Southeast Asia</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Southeast <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asia">Asia</a> is the region comprising mainland states such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cambodia">Cambodia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thailand">Thailand</a> and the islands of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indonesia">Indonesia</a>, Malaysia and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philippines">Philippines</a>. It lay on major maritime trade routes between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>. Empires such as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khmer-empire">Khmer</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/srivijaya">Srivijaya</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/majapahit-empire">Majapahit</a> arose there, and it was influenced by Indian culture under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gupta-empire">Gupta Empire</a> and later occupied by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/empire-of-japan">Empire of Japan</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/southeast-asia.jpg" alt="Southeast Asia" width="320" height="321" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Keepscases · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Southeast_Asia_(orthographic_projection).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
